# AURION Update Server
#
# Copy to .env. start-update-server.cmd does that for you on first run
# and fills ADMIN_TOKEN with a fresh random one, so in practice you only
# come here to change something.

# The password the admin panel asks for. Anyone holding it can publish
# an update to every installed copy of AURION, so treat it like one.
# Make another:  powershell -Command "[guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')"
ADMIN_TOKEN=

# The panel lives at /admin/<this> and is linked from nowhere. That is
# the only thing keeping it off a scanner's list, so change it.
ADMIN_PANEL_HASH=aurion-update-admin-x9k3

# Where the server listens. The launcher prints the full panel URL.
PORT=8898

# Where releases and uploaded files are kept, relative to update-server/.
DATA_DIR=data
